WEBVTT

NOTE station-zero: written VO text from episode.json, timed from the timeline VO placements

V0-1
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.105
Zero means the calculation
asked for no water.

V0-2
00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:07.970
Four checks, in order, tell
you whether that is right.

V1a-1
00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:18.704
When measured VWC is comfortably
above the station target,

V1a-2
00:00:18.804 --> 00:00:22.387
the required amount is zero,
and so is the suggestion.

V1b-1
00:00:22.923 --> 00:00:27.751
Station 10AP1 read 34.5
percent against a target of 16.

V1b-2
00:00:27.851 --> 00:00:32.943
It does not need water today,
so zero is the right answer.

V2a-1
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:42.171
With Set to zero when
pushed to Lynx selected,

V2a-2
00:00:42.271 --> 00:00:45.757
a small but genuine adjustment
is written to Lynx as 0 percent.

V2b-1
00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:50.222
The table still shows the raw value,
so the two disagree. Switch to the

V2b-2
00:00:50.322 --> 00:00:54.400
minimum threshold value option if you
want those stations to keep running.

V3a-1
00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.651
A station with the Enable switch
off is left out of every push,

V3a-2
00:01:05.751 --> 00:01:09.000
so Lynx keeps whatever percent
adjust it already holds.

V3b-1
00:01:09.513 --> 00:01:15.649
Its suggestion is still calculated and
shown, so being disabled does not by

V3b-2
00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:22.213
itself explain a zero. Station 5AP1 is
disabled; the switch on its row is grey.

V4a-1
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:33.512
A scan date older than today means
the reading is stale. Spatial Adjust

V4a-2
00:01:33.612 --> 00:01:38.520
falls back to the modelled value,
in grey italics with a calculator icon.

V4b-1
00:01:39.073 --> 00:01:44.300
Station 7AP1 shows a modelled value,
grey and italic, dated two days ago.

V4b-2
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.413
If the whole course is stale,
TurfRad has not delivered new scans yet.

V5a-1
00:01:55.973 --> 00:01:59.376
If nothing above explains it,
open the diagnostics dialog by

V5a-2
00:01:59.476 --> 00:02:02.823
holding Shift and Alt and
clicking the Spatial Adjust logo.

V5b-1
00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:08.413
It reports whether the org has TurfRad
access, whether it has scan data at all,

V5b-2
00:02:08.513 --> 00:02:11.703
the last scan date, and
whether Lynx is reachable.
